UNIT canonical_string
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 d84d2cbeedc82e13cfbf4fe434f58f7b53d137ea6b6d76e27b14abff858f7633
SIG canonical_string(value) -> string
NOTE default export
ABI json = a JS value: text=string (UTF-16 code units); bool=boolean; list=Array; map=a plain object (prototype
  Object.prototype or null) with own enumerable string keys; f64=number and none=null, both of which throw (R8). Result
  text=string. A throw (R5, R8, widening) is an Error thrown out of the call; the message is free. The artifact is an
  ES module default-exporting the function; it must not import rederive or any package.
ENVELOPE widening: undefined, Array holes, bigint, symbols, functions and every non-plain object (Map, Set, RegExp, Date,
  boxed primitives, typed arrays, class instances) throw; strings holding unpaired surrogates render (JSON.stringify
  escapes them); Object.create(null) is a map. A "__proto__" own key is OUT (the legacy oracle codec turns it into a
  prototype). The R10 probes (raw depth up to 417, beyond the neutral codec's 100 value levels) are graded HERE, through
  the extension oracles/canonical_string.js.json; the default Node stack carries them.
MECHANISM text (R1) and every key = JSON.stringify(string): since ES2019 it realizes TABLE ESCAPE exactly, unpaired
  surrogates as lower-case \uXXXX, U+2028/U+2029 raw. Never JSON.stringify anything else (it would render numbers and
  null instead of throwing, and would neither sort nor project).
MECHANISM list (R2) = Array.isArray; check every index with "i in x" and throw on a hole BEFORE mapping (map skips holes
  and join would render them empty). map (R3) = typeof 'object', not an Array, prototype Object.prototype or null;
  keys = Object.keys(o).sort() (the default sort IS the 16-bit code-unit order of R4). Projections (R5, R6): test
  x.t === 'f64' / 'throw' first, validate bits with HEX16, then render a fresh { t: 'f64', bits } or { t: 'throw' } so the
  dropped entries are never visited. Anything else (number, null, undefined, bigint, symbol, function, other object) throws.
DEPENDS-ON none
MECHANISM R10: carry the node depth down the recursion (the top call at 0) and throw before rendering a node deeper than
  416 (the check first, before the type tests); check it at every visited node, the projected "bits"/"t" text included, never at keys or dropped entries.
PINNED regex HEX16 = /^[0-9a-f]{16}$/ CITED R5 — the bits accept-set
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/sir/canon.mjs canonicalString (own code). Round 5 language file, 2026-10-27; the widening
  and R10 vectors live in oracles/canonical_string.js.json (tooling-routed).
